WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.620
"Was that Mrs. Sweet?" Jackson raced down the alley.

2
00:00:17.621 --> 00:00:19.471
Henry and Maggie followed.

3
00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:22.998
The alley was between the Sweet Shop and another store.

4
00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:25.433
At the back was a small shed.

5
00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:31.241
Mrs. Sweet stood there facing Miss Bishop, who owned the jewelry store across the street.

6
00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:36.129
"Oh my, Laura!" Miss Bishop fanned her face with one hand.

7
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:40.105
"You nearly gave me a heart attack sneaking up on me like that!"

8
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:44.185
"I wasn't sneaking, Jane," Mrs. Sweet retorted.

9
00:00:44.186 --> 00:00:49.366
"I was just walking to my shed. What were you doing back here anyway?

10
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.401
Trying to get a peek at my float, hmm?"

11
00:00:52.402 --> 00:00:57.618
"Of course not!" Just then Miss Bishop noticed Henry and the others.

12
00:00:57.619 --> 00:01:00.029
"Oh, hello."

13
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.627
"Is everything all right, ladies?" Jackson asked. "We heard a scream."

14
00:01:04.628 --> 00:01:10.492
"That was me." Miss Bishop smiled. "Mrs. Sweet startled me."

15
00:01:10.493 --> 00:01:13.520
Henry traded an amused look with Maggie.

16
00:01:13.521 --> 00:01:17.591
They both knew that Miss Bishop was a very dramatic person.

17
00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:22.610
"I see," Jackson said. "Mrs. Sweet, can I talk to you?"

18
00:01:22.611 --> 00:01:27.809
"Of course." Mrs. Sweet shot Miss Bishop a suspicious look.

19
00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.620
"Just let me lock my shed first.

20
00:01:30.621 --> 00:01:35.308
I wouldn't want anyone wandering in and getting a look at my float."

21
00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:42.330
Miss Bishop rolled her eyes. "Why would anyone want to do that?"

22
00:01:42.331 --> 00:01:45.136
Soon Miss Bishop returned to her shop.

23
00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:50.640
Henry, Maggie, Jackson, and Mrs. Sweet headed into the Sweet Shop.

24
00:01:50.641 --> 00:01:54.767
"I heard you had some trouble last night," Jackson said to Mrs. Sweet.

25
00:01:54.768 --> 00:01:59.246
He pulled out a notebook and pen. "Someone broke into your shed?"

26
00:01:59.247 --> 00:02:05.309
"Yes." Mrs. Sweet shook her head. "It was a terrible shock."

27
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:10.493
"What happened?" Maggie blurted out. "Did someone sabotage your float?"

28
00:02:10.494 --> 00:02:14.242
"I'm not sure." Mrs. Sweet looked troubled.

29
00:02:14.243 --> 00:02:20.501
"I left the shed unlocked last night so Mr. Newman could stop by on his way home from work.

30
00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:24.344
I needed him to fix the taillight on my tractor."

31
00:02:24.345 --> 00:02:28.754
"Mr. Newman from the auto repair shop?" Henry asked.

32
00:02:28.755 --> 00:02:31.999
"Yes, that's right," Mrs. Sweet said.

33
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.665
"He's a good mechanic, isn't he?

34
00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:38.683
In any case, I went to check the float this morning.

35
00:02:38.684 --> 00:02:43.434
The taillight was fixed, but a whole case of candy was missing!"

36
00:02:43.435 --> 00:02:46.783
"Candy?" Jackson looked confused.

37
00:02:46.784 --> 00:02:50.223
"Yes." Mrs. Sweet leaned forward.

38
00:02:50.224 --> 00:02:55.095
"I was going to use it to decorate my float," she whispered.

39
00:02:55.096 --> 00:02:58.217
Henry covered his mouth to hide his smile.

40
00:02:58.218 --> 00:03:02.964
Mrs. Sweet was whispering, acting as if everything was top secret.

41
00:03:02.965 --> 00:03:07.213
But she decorated her float with candy every single year!

42
00:03:07.214 --> 00:03:11.848
"There have been some problems with raccoons around town lately," Jackson said.

43
00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:14.156
"Or perhaps a stray dog."

44
00:03:14.157 --> 00:03:18.329
"I don't think it was an animal." Mrs. Sweet said, frowning.

45
00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.000
"The shed door wasn't locked, but it was shut tightly.

46
00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:25.263
The latch can only be opened by a person."

47
00:03:25.264 --> 00:03:30.721
"I see." Jackson jotted a few notes, and then tucked his notebook away.

48
00:03:30.722 --> 00:03:36.062
"Well, give me a call if you think of anything else."

49
00:03:36.063 --> 00:03:40.285
Henry and Maggie followed the reporter outside.

50
00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:45.305
"Is that it?" Maggie asked. "Aren't you going to examine the crime scene?"

51
00:03:45.306 --> 00:03:50.234
Jackson looked surprised. "That's a job for the police, not for me."

52
00:03:50.235 --> 00:03:54.774
"But we thought you'd want to get to the bottom of the story," Henry said.

53
00:03:54.775 --> 00:03:57.761
"Why don't you go interview Mr. Newman?"

54
00:03:57.762 --> 00:04:01.120
Jackson shrugged. "I suppose I could.

55
00:04:01.121 --> 00:04:06.906
The auto repair shop is on my way back to the office."

56
00:04:06.907 --> 00:04:10.184
Soon the three of them were at Newman's Auto Shop.

57
00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:13.285
Henry had known Mr. Newman all his life.

58
00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:19.598
Henry's parents said the people of Belltown were lucky to have such an honest and hardworking mechanic in town.

59
00:04:19.599 --> 00:04:22.880
Mr. Newman listened to why Jackson was there.

60
00:04:22.881 --> 00:04:27.582
"What do you want to know?" he asked in his usual gruff way.

61
00:04:27.583 --> 00:04:32.255
"Did you stop by to fix Mrs. Sweet's taillight last night?" Jackson asked.

62
00:04:32.256 --> 00:04:36.640
Mr. Newman nodded. "Fixed the light and then went home."

63
00:04:36.641 --> 00:04:40.676
"Did you see a case of candy near the float?" Maggie asked.

64
00:04:40.677 --> 00:04:45.373
"Didn't notice. I was there to fix the light, not to sightsee."

65
00:04:45.374 --> 00:04:50.889
Mr. Newman checked his watch. "Is there anything else? I have work to do."

66
00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:55.101
"No, there's nothing else. Thanks for your time," Jackson said.

67
00:04:55.102 --> 00:04:58.647
"Wait," Maggie said as Jackson turned to leave.

68
00:04:58.648 --> 00:05:02.244
"Mr. Newman, are you making a float for the parade?"

69
00:05:02.245 --> 00:05:05.694
Mr. Newman looked surprised. "Of course not.

70
00:05:05.695 --> 00:05:10.411
I don't have time for that sort of silliness." He hurried off.

71
00:05:10.412 --> 00:05:15.383
"Sorry, kids," Jackson said. "It looks like there's no mystery here."

72
00:05:15.384 --> 00:05:18.565
"What about the missing candy?" Maggie asked.

73
00:05:18.566 --> 00:05:21.310
"And that threat?" Henry added.

74
00:05:21.311 --> 00:05:24.920
"Threat? What threat?" Jackson asked.

75
00:05:24.921 --> 00:05:29.167
Henry realized they'd never told the reporter about the comment on the website.

76
00:05:29.168 --> 00:05:31.723
He quickly filled Jackson in.

77
00:05:31.724 --> 00:05:35.340
Jackson pulled out his smartphone and opened the website.

78
00:05:35.341 --> 00:05:37.828
"I don't see any threatening comments."

79
00:05:37.829 --> 00:05:42.530
"I'll show you." Henry took the phone and scrolled through the comments.

80
00:05:42.531 --> 00:05:47.374
The ones from Mrs. Sweet and Miss Bishop were there, along with several others.

81
00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:53.698
But the threatening comment was gone!
